# Java Spring Boot Guidelines
Stack: Java 21, Spring Boot, PostgreSQL (prod), file-based H2 (local; survives restart).
## Package layout
com..ticketmanagement/ config/ controller/ dto/ domain/ repository/ service/ exception/ mapper/


## Layer responsibilities

- Controllers: map HTTP to service calls only; no business logic; no repository injection
- Services: business logic; `@Transactional` on writes; `@Transactional(readOnly = true)` on reads
- Repositories: Spring Data JPA only; derived queries or `@Query` with named parameters; native SQL only when required and justified in a short comment
- Domain: JPA entities only; do not return entities from controllers
- DTOs: Java records for request/response payloads
- Mapping: entity ↔ DTO in `mapper` (MapStruct or manual)

## Java 21

- Use records for DTOs and immutable value types
- Use sealed types for closed hierarchies when the set of variants is fixed
- Use pattern matching for `switch` / `instanceof` when it simplifies branching
- Use text blocks for multi-line strings
- Use `var` only when the type is obvious from the initializer

## Spring practices

- Constructor injection only
- `@Valid` / `@Validated` on controller inputs
- `@Enumerated(EnumType.STRING)` for persisted enums
- Prefer unidirectional JPA relations; add bidirectional only when required
- Prefer Flyway migrations for schema changes; do not use `ddl-auto=update` outside local experiments
- Profiles: `local` uses **file-based H2** (`./data/ticketdb`, not in-memory); `prod` uses PostgreSQL
- Do not switch local to `jdbc:h2:mem:...` — it breaks restart persistence acceptance
- Externalize secrets and environment-specific values; never hardcode credentials
- Log with SLF4J; never log secrets or PII
- Prefer `Optional.orElseThrow` / `map` / `ifPresent`; do not call `Optional.get()` unsafely

## Agent behavior

- Match existing package names and patterns once code exists
- Prefer small, reviewable changes
- New feature path: DTO → service → repository → migration when schema changes